=== []
exit 2
--- stdout
toolportctl: manage Toolport+ from the command line

Usage: toolportctl [--json] [--data-dir <dir>] <command> [args]

Commands:
  status         Show registry, profile, secrets backend and gateway state
  doctor         Run read-only health checks
  server ls      List servers and whether the active profile enables them
  server search  Search the catalog (--offline, --limit <n>)
  server install Install a catalog server by name
  server uninstall Remove a server and its client entries (--dry-run)
  server info    Show one server's definition and profiles
  server new     Add a custom server (--command or --url)
  server edit    Edit a server's name, command, args, url or cwd
  inspect        List the tools a server exposes (connects live)
  profile inspect List the tools of every server in a profile (connects live)
  profile        Profiles (not implemented)
  client ls      List detected clients and their direct entries
  client sync    Sync managed clients (--client <id>, --dry-run, --keep-orphans)
  client         Client configs (not implemented)
  server         Manage servers (mutations) (not implemented)
  auth statusline Compact auth-health JSON for a Claude Code statusline
  auth hook      Auth-health JSON for a Claude Code SessionStart hook
  auth           Auth health (not implemented)
  secret set     Store a secret read from stdin or --value-env
  secret get     Check a secret (--reveal prints the value)
  secret rm      Remove a secret
  secret         Manage server secrets (not implemented)
  context loads  Show what a claude session loads, with token cost (--profile, --cwd)
  context folders Show the active profile per folder (--cwd, --enable, --disable)
  context checkpoint-status Report used tokens vs the checkpoint point from statusline JSON on stdin
  context plan   Preview the context deploy (--home <dir>, --rules)
  context apply  Apply the context deploy (--home <dir>, --rules, --no-persist, --dry-run)
  context sync   Plan then apply the context deploy (--home <dir>, --rules, --dry-run)
  context        Context: loads checkpoint-status plan apply sync
  compression status Show the compression policy, pin and drift
  compression presets List presets (--refresh re-snapshots knobs, --dry-run)
  compression enable Enable a provider (--provider, --port, --telemetry, --preset, --mode, --dry-run)
  compression disable Disable compression (--teardown, --dry-run)
  compression set-provider Swap the active provider and re-apply (--dry-run)
  compression use Switch the active preset and re-apply (--dry-run)
  compression sync Re-apply the policy: shims, env snippet, MCP entry (--mcpm-root, --dry-run)
  compression pin Show or set the exact engine pin (--install, --refresh, --dry-run)
  compression seal Declare the live proxy posture as policy (--apply, --dry-run)
  compression env Print the proxy env for a directory, for eval (--cwd)
  compression doctor Run the compression health checks
  compression run Launch claude under the directory's policy (--plan to preview)
  compression verify Check provider health, pin, shims and measure cache behaviour
  compression ledger Launch and token-savings ledger (summary | record)
  compression proxy Proxy lifecycle: up, down, restart
  compression update Move the engine pin (--to V | --latest, --accept to apply)
  compression    Compression: status presets enable disable set-provider use sync pin seal env doctor run verify ledger proxy update
  import mcpm    Import an mcpm config root (--dry-run prints the plan)
  import rename-refs Rewrite mcp__mcpm_ tool references under --paths (--tools F, --dry-run)
  import         Import data from other tools (not implemented)
  council        Council server: install uninstall doctor tools
  mcp            Self-management server: install [--profile <id>] uninstall doctor tools
  skills sync    Transpile skills to client outputs (--repo, --home, --client, --project, --dry-run)
  skills ls      List skills and rules (--repo <dir>, --home <dir>)
  skills lint    Lint skills; exits 1 on errors (--repo, --home, --name <skill>)
  skills diff    Compare skills with the lockfile; exits 1 on changes (--repo, --home)
  skills init    Create a skills repository (--path <dir>, --name <name>, --dry-run)
  skills add     Create a skill or rule from a template (<name>, --type, --path, --with-progressive, --dry-run)
  skills audit   Scan skills for prompt injection and risky commands; exits 1 on high findings (--path <dir>)
  skills bundle  Pack skills into a portable zip (--output <zip>, --path <dir>, --skills <a,b>, --dry-run)
  skills unbundle Extract a skills bundle (<bundle.zip>, --path <dir>, --dry-run)
  skills status  Show whether synced outputs still exist; --strict exits 1 on drift (--repo, --home, --client <key>)
  skills clean   Remove synced outputs and the lockfile (--repo, --home, --client <key>, --project, --dry-run)
  skills uninstall Remove a skill, its outputs and its lock entry (<name>, --repo, --home, --project, --dry-run)
  skills resolve Find files shadowing synced skills; --migrate backs them up (--repo, --home, --client <key>, --project, --dry-run)
  skills         Skills: init add ls lint audit bundle unbundle sync diff status clean uninstall resolve
  sync           Encrypted sync: init push pull diff status reset ...
  cc             Claude Code plugins: list | update [--dry-run]
  update         Check or apply server updates (--check, --apply, --init, --dry-run)
  usage          Token and MCP usage from Claude Code transcripts (--root <dir>, --no-refresh)

Options:
  --json             Machine-readable envelope on stdout
  --data-dir <dir>   Override the data directory (default: TOOLPORT_DATA_DIR)
  -h, --help         Show this help
  -V, --version      Show the version

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage
--- stderr
